      "domain": "industrial_quality_control",
      "title": "industrial quality control method",
      "summary": "An industrial line used Wald's sequential probability ratio test for Bernoulli defects. After n trials with x defects, it computed log LR=x*ln(p1/p0)+(n-x)*ln((1-p1)/(1-p0)). It accepted p1 if log LR >= ln((1-beta)/alpha), accepted p0 if log LR <= ln(beta/(1-alpha)), and otherwise continued sampling.",
